/T (This report presents the complete implementation of a real-time object tracking system using OpenCV. It covers all stages of the pipeline, including video acquisition, preprocessing, CSRT-based tracking, trajectory generation, and performance evaluation. The system is designed to operate using Python 3.x and OpenCV libraries, without the use of deep learning frameworks such as TensorFlow or PyTorch. It processes video input from files or camera streams and outputs annotated frames with bounding boxes and trajectory paths. The report also includes experimental results demonstrating tracking performance on traffic video datasets. The system is intended for applications such as traffic monitoring, surveillance, and motion analysis, where real-time object tracking is required using lightweight and efficient computational methods.)
/E (This report presents the complete implementation of a real-time object tracking system using OpenCV. It covers all stages of the pipeline, including video acquisition, preprocessing, CSRT-based tracking, trajectory generation, and performance evaluation. The system is designed to operate using Python 3.x and OpenCV libraries, without the use of deep learning frameworks such as TensorFlow or PyTorch. It processes video input from files or camera streams and outputs annotated frames with bounding boxes and trajectory paths. The report also includes experimental results demonstrating tracking performance on traffic video datasets. The system is intended for applications such as traffic monitoring, surveillance, and motion analysis, where real-time object tracking is required using lightweight and efficient computational methods.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
