399 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 146 0 R
/T (5.1 Algorithm Overview The system implements a single-stream tracking architecture based on the CSRT \(Discriminative Correlation Filter with Channel and Spatial Reliability\) algorithm. The process begins with bounding box initialization around the target object, followed by continuous frame-by-frame tracking using correlation filters and spatial reliability mapping. The tracker updates the object position dynamically while adapting to scale and appearance changes. The centroid of the bounding box is computed for each frame to generate a trajectory path, enabling motion analysis and tracking visualization.)
/E (5.1 Algorithm Overview The system implements a single-stream tracking architecture based on the CSRT \(Discriminative Correlation Filter with Channel and Spatial Reliability\) algorithm. The process begins with bounding box initialization around the target object, followed by continuous frame-by-frame tracking using correlation filters and spatial reliability mapping. The tracker updates the object position dynamically while adapting to scale and appearance changes. The centroid of the bounding box is computed for each frame to generate a trajectory path, enabling motion analysis and tracking visualization.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
400 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 146 0 R
/T (5.2 CSRT Tracker Initialization The CSRT tracker is initialized by selecting a region of interest \(ROI\) around the target object in the initial video frame. This region is defined using a bounding box specified by its position and dimensions. The tracker extracts feature representations from this region, including color and texture information, and constructs correlation filters based on channel and spatial reliability. These filters enable the tracker to distinguish the object from the background. Proper initialization is critical, as it directly influences tracking accuracy and stability throughout the video sequence.)
/E (5.2 CSRT Tracker Initialization The CSRT tracker is initialized by selecting a region of interest \(ROI\) around the target object in the initial video frame. This region is defined using a bounding box specified by its position and dimensions. The tracker extracts feature representations from this region, including color and texture information, and constructs correlation filters based on channel and spatial reliability. These filters enable the tracker to distinguish the object from the background. Proper initialization is critical, as it directly influences tracking accuracy and stability throughout the video sequence.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
