/P 148 0 R
/T (The trajectory tracking mechanism records the motion path of the tracked object by computing its centroid position in each frame. The centroid is calculated from the bounding box and appended to a list that maintains the recent movement history. As new frames are processed, consecutive centroid points are connected using line segments to form a continuous trajectory path. To ensure clarity and efficiency, the trajectory length is limited to a fixed number of points, discarding older positions. This approach provides a visual representation of object movement, enabling analysis of direction, displacement, and motion patterns while maintaining real-time performance and stability.)
/E (The trajectory tracking mechanism records the motion path of the tracked object by computing its centroid position in each frame. The centroid is calculated from the bounding box and appended to a list that maintains the recent movement history. As new frames are processed, consecutive centroid points are connected using line segments to form a continuous trajectory path. To ensure clarity and efficiency, the trajectory length is limited to a fixed number of points, discarding older positions. This approach provides a visual representation of object movement, enabling analysis of direction, displacement, and motion patterns while maintaining real-time performance and stability.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
