1120 0 obj
<<
/Title (This project presents the design, implementation, and evaluation of a real-time moving object detection and trajectory tracking system using classical computer vision techniques in Python with OpenCV. The system utilizes the CSRT \(Discriminative Correlation Filter with Channel and Spatial Reliability\) tracker, a robust tracking algorithm capable of handling scale variation, occlusion, and background noise in dynamic environments such as traffic surveillance videos.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1114 0 R
/Next 1126 0 R
>>
endobj
1121 0 obj
<<
/Title (The complete system is lightweight, requires no GPU or deep learning framework, and is implemented using only standard Python libraries such as OpenCV and NumPy. It can process video frames in near real-time and is suitable for applications such as traffic monitoring, surveillance, and motion analysis.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1114 0 R
/Prev 1127 0 R
>>
endobj
