/Title (2.2 Deep Learning Approaches Deep learning approaches to object detection and tracking have gained significant attention following the success of convolutional neural networks such as AlexNet \(2012\). CNN-based models, including Faster R-CNN and YOLO, have demonstrated high accuracy in detecting and tracking objects in complex scenes. Redmon et al. \(2016\) introduced YOLO, which enables real-time object detection with impressive speed and accuracy. Subsequent versions, such as YOLOv5 and YOLOv8, further improved detection performance and efficiency in real-world applications. In tracking, deep learning-based methods often combine detection with tracking frameworks, such as SORT and Deep SORT, to maintain object identities across frames. While these approaches achieve high accuracy, they require large annotated datasets and GPU-based computation for real-time performance. In contrast, classical methods like CSRT provide a lightweight alternative suitable for CPU-based systems without extensive training requirements.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1140 0 R
/Prev 1145 0 R
/Next 1146 0 R
