/Title (Integration of deep learning-based object detection \(e.g., YOLO\) to enable automatic initialization and fully autonomous multi-object tracking. Deep learning hybrid: Training a lightweight MobileNetV3 classifier on the detected pothole and crack patches would reduce the false positive rate from the classical detection streams without requiring full frame-level deep learning inference, maintaining CPU deployability. Depth camera integration: Combining the 2D Laplacian blob detection with structured-light depth maps from a RealSense or Kinect camera would enable volumetric pothole depth and volume estimation, providing a more precise repair cost estimate than area-only severity scoring. Temporal consistency: Averaging defect mask confidence over a 10-frame sliding window in continuous video processing mode would reduce flickering false positives caused by transient illumination changes \(vehicle headlight reflections, passing shadows\). Incorporation of a re-detection mechanism to recover from tracking failure when the object is lost or re-enters the frame.)
/Dest [27 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1150 0 R
>>
endobj
