/Title (3.2 Annotation and Trajectory Analysis For quantitative evaluation, ground-truth tracking was approximated by manually initializing bounding boxes around the target object in the initial frame and visually verifying tracking consistency across subsequent frames. The object position in each frame was represented by the centroid of the bounding box, enabling frame-wise trajectory generation. These trajectory points serve as reference data for evaluating tracking stability and motion continuity. Tracking performance was assessed using metrics such as success rate and frame-wise accuracy based on whether the object remained correctly localized. Additionally, qualitative evaluation was performed by comparing the generated trajectory path with the actual object movement. This approach enables reliable assessment without requiring labelled datasets or complex annotation tools.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1154 0 R
/Prev 1159 0 R
>>
