/Title (5.1 Algorithm Overview The system implements a single-stream tracking architecture based on the CSRT \(Discriminative Correlation Filter with Channel and Spatial Reliability\) algorithm. The process begins with bounding box initialization around the target object, followed by continuous frame-by-frame tracking using correlation filters and spatial reliability mapping. The tracker updates the object position dynamically while adapting to scale and appearance changes. The centroid of the bounding box is computed for each frame to generate a trajectory path, enabling motion analysis and tracking visualization.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1198 0 R
/Next 1206 0 R
>>
endobj
