/Title (5.2 CSRT Tracker Initialization The CSRT tracker is initialized by selecting a region of interest \(ROI\) around the target object in the initial video frame. This region is defined using a bounding box specified by its position and dimensions. The tracker extracts feature representations from this region, including color and texture information, and constructs correlation filters based on channel and spatial reliability. These filters enable the tracker to distinguish the object from the background. Proper initialization is critical, as it directly influences tracking accuracy and stability throughout the video sequence.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1198 0 R
/Prev 1203 0 R
/Next 1204 0 R
>>
